===Proper noun===
{{en-prop}}

# {{senseid|en|Q8641}}A West Germanic, or more specifically High German, language that developed from [[Middle High German]] dialects, with an admixture of vocabulary from multiple source languages including Hebrew-Aramaic, Romance, Slavic, English, etc., and mostly written in [[Hebrew]] characters which is used mainly among [[Ashkenazi]]c [[Jew]]s from central and eastern Europe.
#: {{syn|en|Jewish}}
#: {{holo|en|High German}}
#: {{meronyms|en|Eastern Yiddish|East Yiddish|Western Yiddish|West Yiddish}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1983|author=Philip Baldi|title=An Introduction to the Indo-European Languages|page=128
|passage='''Yiddish''' is a High German language [...] two varieties of Yiddish developed [...]}}

